  "agent": {
    "note": "TWO FIXES from candidate-005 feedback. (1) FADE: rows/washes/surface were visible at t=0 because a static overlay.alpha made wrapFade skip them. Fixed by BAKING the wash into a solid tile color (blend) so it fades WITH its row, + fading the card surface from t=0. t=0 is now fully black in every aspect; everything cascades in. (2) VERTICAL RE-LAYOUT: a wide 5-col table can't fit portrait, so portrait (H > W*1.15) now reflows to the SaaS mobile-leaderboard pattern — per-contributor stacked cards: rank | square avatar | name + the ranked metric (col 0) BIG on the right with a label, and secondary columns as a colored diff line below (+additions green / -deletions red via new optional columnColors/columnSigns props). Fixed width-capped fonts (no fit:contain clip). Landscape/square keep the approved table UNCHANGED. Scales clean 720x1280 -> 1080x1920. This file is portrait so you see the new layout; open in Make and switch aspect to spot-check the table too.",
    "question": "Portrait stacked-card layout good? (avatar still a rounded chip — circle is a separate open question.) Anything to nudge — the repeated 'Commits' label under each big number, card spacing, the diff-line indent? If good, I lock the primitive (unit test + master gate) and compose Beat 3.",
    "response": {
      "body": "for square, the icon next to top contributors isnt square here and should be. Also lets color additions green and deletions red and add the + and -, like mobile now has.\n\nmobile layout looks great.\n\ndesktop is fine, except same with icon ne to top contrib id like to be square. and same update for additons and deletions",
